{"id":"H7301","lemma":"רָוָה","transliteration":"ravah","sayIt":"RA-vah","language":"Hebrew","partOfSpeech":"verb","gloss":"to quench","meaning":"1) to be satiated or saturated, have or drink one's fill\n1a) (Qal) to take one's fill\n1b) (Piel)\n1b1) to be drunk, be intoxicated\n1b2) to drench, water abundantly, saturate\n1c) (Hiphil) to saturate, water, cause to drink","glosses":["feast on","soak","satisfy you","let us take our fill","who refreshes others","drench"],"count":14,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"psa-36","v":8,"renderings":{"bsb":"They feast on","kjv":"They shall be abundantly satisfied"}},{"chapterId":"psa-65","v":10,"renderings":{"bsb":"You soak","kjv":"Thou waterest"}},{"chapterId":"pro-5","v":19,"renderings":{"bsb":"satisfy you","kjv":"satisfy"}},{"chapterId":"pro-7","v":18,"renderings":{"bsb":"let us take our fill","kjv":"let us take our fill"}},{"chapterId":"pro-11","v":25,"renderings":{"bsb":"and he who refreshes others","kjv":"and he that watereth"}},{"chapterId":"isa-16","v":9,"renderings":{"bsb":"I drench","kjv":"I will water"}},{"chapterId":"isa-34","v":5,"renderings":{"bsb":"has drunk its fill","kjv":"shall be bathed"}},{"chapterId":"isa-34","v":7,"renderings":{"bsb":"will be drenched","kjv":"shall be soaked"}},{"chapterId":"isa-43","v":24,"renderings":{"bsb":"satisfied Me","kjv":"neither hast thou filled"}},{"chapterId":"isa-55","v":10,"renderings":{"bsb":"watering","kjv":"but watereth"}},{"chapterId":"jer-31","v":14,"renderings":{"bsb":"I will fill","kjv":"And I will satiate"}},{"chapterId":"jer-31","v":25,"renderings":{"bsb":"I will refresh","kjv":"For I have satiated"}},{"chapterId":"jer-46","v":10,"renderings":{"bsb":"until it is quenched","kjv":"and made drunk"}},{"chapterId":"lam-3","v":15,"renderings":{"bsb":"He has intoxicated me","kjv":"he hath made me drunken"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Psalm 36:8","note":"They shall be abundantly satisfied with the abundance of your house. You will make them drink of the river of your pleasures.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Proverbs 5:19","note":"A loving doe and a graceful deer— let her breasts satisfy you at all times. Be captivated always with her love.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Isaiah 16:9","note":"Therefore I will weep with the weeping of Jazer for the vine of Sibmah. I will water you with my tears, Heshbon, and Elealeh: for on your summer fruits and on…","source":"web"},{"ref":"Jeremiah 31:14","note":"I will satiate the soul of the priests with fatness, and my people will be satisfied with my goodness,” says Yahweh.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Lamentations 3:15","note":"He has filled me with bitterness. He has stuffed me with wormwood.","source":"web"}],"related":[],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}